  "description": "WCAG 2.2 AA contrast of form themes: colour pairs with their contrast ratio, and themes with the pairings that fail and the nearest colours that pass. Run by backend/tests/app/services/test_theme_contrast.py (services/theme_contrast.py, the publish check theme_contrast) and webapp src/utils/theme-contrast-cases.test.ts (utils/color-contrast.ts, themeContrastGuard in utils/theme-contrast.ts), so the builder's guard and the server's publish check can't drift. 'ratio' to 6 decimals (null: a colour that is not hex, which fails every check); 'display' is the ratio as shown, one decimal rounded down. Text needs 4.5:1, controls 3:1. A theme's 'issues' are in the order text, answer, button, border, action, each at its lowest ratio; 'fix' holds only the keys that change (null when nothing fails); an image page can't be measured ('imageGround'). Every preset is listed and passes.",
